  "_note": "Levels for The Pushing Floor. Every one must pass verify_levels.mjs, which asks TWO questions: is it solvable, and is it solvable WITHOUT the letters. A level that passes the first and fails the second is a level where the letters are decoration. Coordinates are [x, y, z]; y is 0 throughout — this is a floor.",
  "how_it_works": {
    "walk": "The scribe steps north/south/east/west and shoves what is in front. A bonded body moves as a whole or not at all.",
    "inscribe": "A letter from the hand is written into any empty cell the scribe can reach, and stays there. It is spent.",
    "bind": "A closed letter joins the two cells across the writing line — for the default westward line, the cells one step north and one step south of it. Those two become one body.",
    "axis": "A letter that holds a frame will not be shoved, and nothing bonded to it will be either."
  },
